    {
      "id": "riv-lowfires",
      "type": "adventure",
      "x": 6600,
      "speaker": "",
      "lines": [
        "The low fires are small and there are many of them, strung along the shingle where the river widens and goes quiet.",
        "People sit at them in twos and threes, facing the road rather than the water. They look up when anyone comes down the rise. They have done this many times.",
        "At the fire nearest the water, someone stands."
      ],
      "choices": [
        "Go down"
      ],
      "responses": [
        "Whoever walked out of the meadow did not walk down to the fires. Everyone who did is standing behind you."
      ],
